{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0125Gehcch4JPeZzNWoSZQSz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence Murday Cotts\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/\"},{\"title\":\"s00231 011 0874 9\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9\"},{\"title\":\"link.springer.com\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553\"},{\"title\":\"jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp\",\"url\":\"https://jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp/records/41864\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium\",\"url\":\"https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5\"},{\"title\":\"Quasielastic neutron scattering and diffusion in liquid lithium and lithium–hydrogen melt\",\"url\":\"https://hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr/insu-00332070\"},{\"title\":\"Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering\",\"url\":\"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0\"},{\"title\":\"repository.ias.ac.in\",\"url\":\"https://repository.ias.ac.in/56008/\"},{\"title\":\"informahealthcare.com\",\"url\":\"https://informahealthcare.com/doi/abs/10.1080/14786430802422006\"},{\"title\":\"subject:Self diffusion coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the Murday and Cotts paper but not its actual numbers, so I couldn't confirm their temperature-dependence parameters.\n\n- **Source paper:** Murday and Cotts (1968), \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" *J Chem Phys* 48:4938–4945, appears in a reference list from a 2012 paper ([link.springer.com](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9)).\n- **Agreement with later work:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study using an EAM potential reports that its calculated self-diffusion coefficients agree with Murday's experimental results at atmospheric pressure. It also finds the coefficient rises with temperature and derives an Arrhenius fit from its simulations ([scholar.xjtu.edu.cn](https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/)).\n- **Other measurements:** Neutron quasielastic scattering on liquid lithium at 500 K and 830 K gave values consistent with the literature ([hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr](https://hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr/insu-00332070)). A 2012 coherent quasielastic neutron study examined the temperature dependence and compared it with incoherent-scattering data ([katalog.lib.cas.cz](https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0)). Feinauer and co-authors published experimental 6Li and 7Li diffusivity data in 1994 ([link.springer.com](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9)).\n- **Isotope effects:** A 1986 pseudopotential analysis explains the unusual ratio between 6Li and 7Li self-diffusion coefficients through the mass dependence of the mean free path ([scilit.com](https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5)).\n\nTo get the Murday–Cotts Arrhenius coefficients, you would need the 1968 paper itself (J. Chem. Phys. 48, 4938), which these results did not include.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce9b779d-8720-4421-9f50-5788bba003fc","uuid":"0f3f3de4-a8b5-46e2-ba6c-ce1c64cc4d92","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:58:03.922Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium self-diffusion coefficient measurement temperature dependence Murday Cotts","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01H593WnzXEBo7ynCm5NXVTZ","content":[{"title":"self diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium","url":"https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/"},{"title":"s00231 011 0874 9","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9"},{"title":"link.springer.com","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF00883553"},{"title":"jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp","url":"https://jaxa.repo.nii.ac.jp/records/41864"},{"title":"Self-diffusion and isotopic effects in liquid lithium","url":"https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5"},{"title":"Quasielastic neutron scattering and diffusion in liquid lithium and lithium–hydrogen melt","url":"https://hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr/insu-00332070"},{"title":"Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering","url":"https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0"},{"title":"repository.ias.ac.in","url":"https://repository.ias.ac.in/56008/"},{"title":"informahealthcare.com","url":"https://informahealthcare.com/doi/abs/10.1080/14786430802422006"},{"title":"subject:Self diffusion coefficients","url":"https://fitforthem.unipa.it/subject:Self-diffusion coefficients"}]},"The search turned up the Murday and Cotts paper but not its actual numbers, so I couldn't confirm their temperature-dependence parameters.\n\n- **Source paper:** Murday and Cotts (1968), \"Self-diffusion coefficient of liquid lithium,\" *J Chem Phys* 48:4938–4945, appears in a reference list from a 2012 paper ([link.springer.com](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9)).\n- **Agreement with later work:** A 2012 molecular-dynamics study using an EAM potential reports that its calculated self-diffusion coefficients agree with Murday's experimental results at atmospheric pressure. It also finds the coefficient rises with temperature and derives an Arrhenius fit from its simulations ([scholar.xjtu.edu.cn](https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/)).\n- **Other measurements:** Neutron quasielastic scattering on liquid lithium at 500 K and 830 K gave values consistent with the literature ([hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr](https://hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr/insu-00332070)). A 2012 coherent quasielastic neutron study examined the temperature dependence and compared it with incoherent-scattering data ([katalog.lib.cas.cz](https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0)). Feinauer and co-authors published experimental 6Li and 7Li diffusivity data in 1994 ([link.springer.com](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9)).\n- **Isotope effects:** A 1986 pseudopotential analysis explains the unusual ratio between 6Li and 7Li self-diffusion coefficients through the mass dependence of the mean free path ([scilit.com](https://scilit.com/publications/a87ad4db2680c466d4fc33f00ce090a5)).\n\nTo get the Murday–Cotts Arrhenius coefficients, you would need the 1968 paper itself (J. Chem. Phys. 48, 4938), which these results did not include."],"durationSeconds":5.659454269000009,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0125Gehcch4JPeZzNWoSZQSz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
