{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb6zLJ18bP8bxSRUQ8Jo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't get a self-diffusion coefficient for liquid lithium at 800 K. I ran out of budget before the production run finished. I posted a `\"failed\"` run report (`000c098e-1457-471a-8315-812fb8efefc2`) under candidate `503075df…` and no value.\n\n- **Premise check:** the task is well-posed. Lithium melts at 453.7 K, so it is a stable liquid at 800 K. Its diffusion coefficient (about 10⁻⁴ cm²/s) can be measured from atomic displacements over roughly 20 ps of constant-energy MD. The team's premise referee had already passed it.\n- **What finished:**\n  - **Lattice-constant check:** the model (MACE-MPA-0) gives 3.430 Å for solid bcc lithium at 0 K. That is about 0.6% below the experimental value of about 3.45 Å, which is typical for the DFT data the model was trained on. This is only a check that the model behaves sensibly for lithium, not the requested check against a known diffusion result.\n  - **Melting:** the 250-atom cell melted at 1500 K.\n- **Why it stopped:** another process was already using the GPU, so each MD step took about 0.19 s. The full sequence (melt, density run at 800 K and zero pressure, short equilibration, 20 ps constant-energy production) needs more than an hour. I cut the protocol to a 2 fs timestep and restarted, but the budget ran out during the density run.\n- **Run still going:** the restarted job may still be running in `/work/run` (process 1145) and could write results there later. Nobody will check or post them, so anything it produces is not a reviewed result.\n- **No reference value:** the calibration file has no lithium entries. The web search pointed to Murday & Cotts, *J. Chem. Phys.* 48, 4938 (1968), but did not give their numbers, so I quoted none.\n\n**To finish it:** rerun `/work/run/li.py` on a GPU nobody else is using (about 45 minutes), then run `/work/run/ana.py`. Before trusting the number, check that energy drift at the 2 fs timestep is small. Also note that `ana.py` assumes a viscosity of 0.33 mPa·s for its finite-size correction, a value I haven't verified, so source a measured viscosity first.\n\nSources:\n- [Self-diffusion coefficient study of liquid lithium (XJTU)](https://scholar.xjtu.edu.cn/en/publications/self-diffusion-coefficient-study-of-liquid-lithium/)\n- [Springer article citing Murday & Cotts 1968](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00231-011-0874-9)\n- [Quasielastic neutron scattering and diffusion in liquid lithium](https://hal-insu.archives-ouvertes.fr/insu-00332070)\n- [Self-diffusion in liquid lithium from coherent quasielastic neutron scattering](https://katalog.lib.cas.cz/KNAV/EdsRecord/edsair,edsair.doi...........2430b859cd2c8ede718b24c249f43fd0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":44633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":950,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":749,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce9b779d-8720-4421-9f50-5788bba003fc","uuid":"e910a256-6e06-4489-9670-1be149b3664d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:28:47.462Z","request_id":"req_011Cgb6zKvvsHXhLdbo6oqDJ"}
